<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI23-IMPORTANT-008>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI23-IMPORTANT-008" ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T06:53:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S3 ;
  triage:title "openapi_surface test never cross-checks live api.rs routes against openapi.yaml, letting route drift ship silently" ;
  triage:description "Surfaced by arch-qa during the AI.23 round-2 recheck. The only automated gate over docs/atm-daemon/openapi.yaml is crates/atm/tests/openapi_surface.rs, which only diffs the YAML against its own prior baseline snapshot (around line 88) - it never cross-checks the live route table in crates/atm-core/src/api.rs (endpoint_for and decode_route_request match arms) against openapi.yaml or ADR-033. This is a structural gap: it is why the PeerSync route in api.rs was able to ship with no corresponding OpenAPI entry, ADR-033 row, or http-api.md row, completely undetected by CI. Reconfirmed by req-qa round 3 (2026-07-26) on feature/pAI-s23-crosshost-shared-write-path @ 985a6d46. Finding remains open and unaddressed. Correction: extend openapi_surface test to parse crates/atm-core/src/api.rs route table (endpoint_for/decode_route_request/HTTP_ROUTE_INVENTORY constant) and assert every live route has a corresponding openapi.yaml entry." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "testing" ;
  triage:severity "Important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "AICH-S11-QA-OPENAPI: verified fixed on commit e474a00c (PR #653, fix/close-out-openapi-crosscheck). crates/atm/tests/openapi_surface.rs::openapi_routes_match_live_router_surface() now derives documented_route_surface() from the OpenAPI server base (all 8 HTTP verbs) and diffs it against atm_core::api::http_route_surface() (the live route table) in both directions in a single assert: missing_from_openapi = live.difference(documented) and undocumented_live_routes = documented.difference(live). Independently confirmed by reading the actual assertion logic (not the self-report) -- both directions are real, non-vacuous checks over live data, not commented out or left permissive. Only crates/atm/tests/openapi_surface.rs was touched in e474a00c. CI: Just lint all-green on all 3 OSes at time of review; Test legs pending." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T00:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-008/fix-closeout-openapi/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-008/pAI-s21/1> ;
